  "indication": "Calves and piglets in the first month of life:Gentamicin is indicated in treatment of infectious diseases caused by Gram-positive (Staphylococcus spp., and some Streptococcus spp.) and particularly by Gram-negative (Escherichia coli, Proteus spp., Pseudomonas spp., Salmonella spp., Shigella spp., ) bacteria sensitive to gentamicin, even if they are secondary to viral infections. In calves and piglets in particular: ▪of the digestive apparatus (bacterial enteritis, neonatal colibacillosis) ▪of the respiratory apparatus (bronchopneumonia, pneumonia) ▪of the tegument (pyoderma, abscesses and septic injuries) ▪septicaemiaHorses:Gentamicin is indicated in horses for the treatment of infections of the lower respiratory tract in horses caused by aerobic Gram-negative bacteria susceptible to gentamicin.",
